// The (k) disposal verb. `take` extracts the row WITH ownership (a
// synthesized <pool-item!> obligation, O2); `give-back` is the discharge —
// the void call in consume position (std/list:free / Connection:close
// idiom). This is the LEGAL flow 690_007's rejection implies: take, use,
// give back, clean compile. Pins that a taken row can be legally disposed,
// and that the discharge is the store's own verb. `insert | row r` per the
// four-heads ruling.

~import std/io
~import std/store

~std/store:create(pool) { hp: i64 }

~std/store:insert(pool) { hp: 9 }
| row r |> std/store:take(pool[r])
    | item i |> std/io:print.ln("took hp {{ i.hp:d }}") |> std/store:give-back(i)
